# transform_chain_guard.vrs — dod transform-chain-guard D9 (v0.137.5): no route chains one transform into another.
# Cases: (a) a second transform while transformed is refused (other unit, same unit) and logged; (b) admin testform
# while transformed is refused ("revert first") instead of reverting + applying in one frame; (c) a phase switch on
# a settled form still works; (d) Morgana (async SnakePhase form): a phase switch right after the transform either
# swaps or says "Still transforming" — never an error — and a retry lands.
# Needs: Chaos has transform unlocks Beatrice and Dracula (named, not indexed: force-transform adds unlocks and shifts
# the indexes); admin rights (ensure runs adminauth).
ensure
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .beelz admin clear-transform Chaos
wait 2
# --- (a) chain refused ---
chat .beelz transform Dracula
expect-reply Transformed into Dracula
wait 3
chat .beelz transform Beatrice
expect-reply Use .beelz revert first, then transform again.
expect-log \[Beelz TXGUARD\] refused route=Activate reason=Active
chat .beelz transform Dracula
expect-reply You're already transformed as that unit.
expect-log \[Beelz TXGUARD\] refused route=Activate reason=SameUnit
# --- (b) testform refused while transformed ---
chat .beelz admin testform wolf
expect-reply Use .beelz revert first, then run testform again.
expect-log \[Beelz TXGUARD\] refused route=FormTest reason=Active
# --- (c) phase switch on a settled form ---
chat .beelz phase 2
expect-reply Phase 2 (Bloodmage) active
shot full dracula-phase2
chat .beelz revert
expect-reply Reverted from
wait 3
# --- (d) Morgana: phase right after the transform ---
chat .beelz admin force-transform Chaos 591725925
chat .beelz phase 2
expect-no-log (\[Error|Exception|at Beelzebub\.)
wait 3
chat .beelz phase 2
chat .beelz phase
expect-reply Currently in phase 2
shot full morgana-phase2
chat .beelz revert
expect-reply Reverted from
expect-no-log (\[Error|Exception|at Beelzebub\.)
